{"accepted_present_character_ids":["character:ted","character:hana_hanezawa","character:mia_hanezawa"],"current_public_scene_state":"Ted, Hana, and Mia are together in the Hanezawa entryway after Ted arrives.","exact_current_source":"Ted steps into the entryway, greets Hana, and asks how dinner went. He mentions that Sakura is away.","exact_writer_prose":"The entryway still held the faint coolness of the early evening, a thin slice of light from the hall spilling over the polished floor. Ted stood just inside the door, his coat still on, one hand loosely holding the strap of his bag, as Hana faced him with a small, easy smile. Behind her, at the edge of the room, Mia leaned quietly against the archway, her arms folded, her gaze soft and patient—just there, part of the warm stillness, saying nothing.\n\nHana tilted her head just slightly, her eyes bright with genuine warmth. She let the silence hold a beat, then spoke. \"It went well,\" she said, her voice low and even, with the kind of considerate calm that filled the space without pushing. \"From my side, it was lovely.\"\n\nThe words hung in the air, simple and complete, as she smiled once more and waited.","hard_boundaries":["Do not invent Ted's action, dialogue, consent, decision, or private state beyond exact current-source text.","Mia remains physically present but backgrounded unless her participation becomes causally necessary.","Sakura is absent; a name or reference never creates physical presence.","Stop at the next meaningful Ted choice and do not close the scene."],"intended_sequence":{"durable_changes":[],"items":[{"causal_parent_item_key":null,"concise_meaning":"Hana warmly conveys that dinner went well from her perspective, without adding unprovided details.","durable_change_keys":[],"evidence_keys":["source:current","evidence:hana_current"],"item_key":"hana_dinner_reply","kind":"dialogue_intent","owner_id":"character:hana_hanezawa","planner_item_keys":[],"protected_user_claim_keys":[],"protected_user